## The roof

::bg{location="roof" time="night"}
::music{action="start" mood="romantic" volume="down"}
@narrator: The hatch lets out onto flat tar and a guard rail nobody trusts. Sol is lying on his back on an army blanket, a star chart weighted with a torch.
::use{component="enter" who="sol"}
@sol{emotion="happy"}: You came. Lie down. The trick is you have to stop trying to see anything.
@narrator: For a while, neither of you says a word. The mast ticks as it cools.
@sol{emotion="fond"}: Thursday night the Perseids peak. Clearest sky in forty years of this log, if Ines's charts are right. They're always right.
@sol{emotion="shy"}: I watch every year. Alone, usually. It's not a big deal.

<branch id="perseids" prompt="He isn't looking at you, very deliberately.">
  <choice id="yes" label="Promise you'll be here Thursday">
    ::set{run.aff.sol += 1}
    ::accept{quest="meteor"}
    @sol{emotion="surprised"}: Yeah? Okay. Okay. Bring a jumper. I'll bring the good blanket.
  </choice>
  <choice id="maybe" label="Say you'll try">
    ::accept{quest="meteor"}
    @sol{emotion="neutral"}: Sure. If you're up. No pressure.
  </choice>
  <choice id="no" label="Say you'll probably be asleep">
    @sol{emotion="sad"}: Fair. The readings don't take themselves.
  </choice>
</branch>
